! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: unlinked informal reasoning cues force annotators to rediscover links and leave downstream tools without reusable explanations.
  + context: Minted as a marked self-derived fallback after A5's external-first search found no project statement of this specific problem.
  + IF:
    Mathematical exposition contains informal cues alongside formal steps.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the source pattern: “These informal cues are not systematically linked to specific steps or objects; without assistance, annotators must rediscover every linkage by hand, and without structure, downstream tools receive only cleaned events with little reusable explanation.” (source: futon3 library/ai4ci/ai-core-function.flexiarg:26-29)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for mechanisms addressing cue linkage.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source class makes the circular provenance mechanically visible.
